  "notes": "Current datasheet rates the LTM 1160-5.2 at 180 t max (over rear, 13.1 m boom, 2.5 m radius); the '160 t' name is legacy. Source table has 12 boom lengths (13.1, 17.6, 22.1, 26.6, 31.1, 35.5, 40, 44.5, 49, 53.5, 58, 62 m); 44.5 m and 53.5 m omitted here. The 13.1 m boom's 'over rear (0°)' (*) sub-column (180/160/139.5 t ...) is NOT included; values here are 360° (max 86 t). 2.5 m radius row dropped (only over-rear value). IMPORTANT: cells in the source are colour-shaded to indicate required VarioBallast radius (legend 4.73 m light / 5.23 m dark); this file does not encode that - check the source chart before using a cell. Outrigger span from p.3: 8306 mm transverse (VarioBase 2446-8306) x 9185 mm longitudinal. Max supporting force 1052 kN (107.3 t) from p.10 (other figure 748 kN/76.3 t). operatingWeight_t = 60 t on-road with 12 t axle loads (0 t or 3.5 t counterweight, p.9); jobsite 82 t with 22.5 t. Max hook height not taken (cover figures 62/78/99 m ambiguous; main boom value not stated as single number). Chart values are gross: per remark 5 (p.39) the weight of hook block and hooks is part of the load and must be deducted. Other counterweight tables (40, 22.5, 14, 3.5 t) on pp.14-17."
